# Fastify path-normalization auth bypass (CVE-2025-69211 / CVE-2026-2293,
# CWE-551). The pre-condition is a FastifyAdapter created with path-normalization
# options (ignoreDuplicateSlashes / ignoreTrailingSlash) — these let Fastify
# canonicalise the url AFTER NestJS guards ran against the raw path. mestjs gap
# #5 (docs/KEUR-COVERAGE-GAPS.md).
id: KEUR-NEST-012
title: Fastify adapter with path-normalization options (auth-bypass surface)
category: security
severity: error
engine: multiline
window: 6
action: warn
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .ts .js
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: (?s)new\s+FastifyAdapter\s*\(\s*\{.{0,200}?ignoreDuplicateSlashes\s*:\s*true
    message: "FastifyAdapter({ ignoreDuplicateSlashes: true }) — Fastify canonicalises the URL AFTER NestJS guards run on the raw path, so a non-canonical path (//orders/admin) bypasses auth (CVE-2026-2293, CWE-551). Upgrade @nestjs/platform-fastify >= 11.1.14 and decide authz on a role claim, not the url."
  - regex: (?s)new\s+FastifyAdapter\s*\(\s*\{.{0,200}?ignoreTrailingSlash\s*:\s*true
    message: "FastifyAdapter({ ignoreTrailingSlash: true }) — path-normalization-after-authorization surface (CVE-2025-69211 / CVE-2026-2293). Upgrade >= 11.1.14; do not authorize on raw url shape."
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Upgrade @nestjs/platform-fastify to >= 11.1.14; keep guards declarative and authorize on an authenticated role claim, never on the request url string."
